-- title:
--   Eichler class set bijects with level-N supersingular places
-- statement:
--   Let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic a prime $q'$, algebraic over $\mathbb{Z}/q'$, let $X_1$ be an elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\kappa$ with no nonzero $q'$-torsion point, and let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ satisfy `IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b q'`, i.e. $a<0$, $b<0$ and, for each height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$, every nonzero element of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ is a unit exactly when $q'\in v$. Let $\Lambda_1\subseteq\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule which is an order maximal among orders containing it, and $\theta_1$ an injective ring homomorphism from the subring generated by the rationally represented endomorphisms of $X_1$ onto $\Lambda_1$. Let $N\neq 0$ with $q'\nmid N$, and let $m$ be a unit of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},\mathrm{fin}}$ such that $m$ and $N\,m^{-1}$ lie in the adelic box $\widehat{\Lambda_1}$ (the additive closure of the $z\otimes\alpha$ with $z\in\Lambda_1$ and $\alpha$ everywhere integral), with $m\widehat{\Lambda_1}m^{-1}\cap\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ again a maximal order; put $R=\Lambda_1\cap m\widehat{\Lambda_1}m^{-1}$ and assume the relative index of $R$ in $\Lambda_1$ is $N$. The assertion is the existence of a bijection $e$ from the double coset set $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]^{\times}\backslash(\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},\mathrm{fin}})^{\times}/\mathrm{Stab}(\widehat{R})$ (the diagonal image acting on the left, the stabiliser of the box of $R$ on the right) onto the set of places of $\kappa(jq,jq_N)$ satisfying `IsSupersingularPlace q' N κ`, with the following property. For every idele unit $x$, every elliptic $W/\kappa$ and nonzero $\chi\colon X_1\to W$ in `rationalHomSet`, and every unit $d$ of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ such that $\theta_1$ carries the kernel ideal set of $\chi$ (those elements of the rational endomorphism ring of the form $\rho\circ\chi$ with $\rho\colon W\to X_1$ rational) onto the quaternionic conjugate of $d\cdot\mathrm{ofFiniteIdele}(\Lambda_1,x)$; and for every elliptic $W'$ and $\psi\colon W\to W'$, $\psi'\colon W'\to W$ in `rationalHomSet` with $\psi'\circ\psi=N$ and $\psi\circ\psi'=N$, such that $\theta_1$ carries the kernel ideal set of $\psi\circ\chi$ onto the conjugate of $d\cdot\mathrm{ofFiniteIdele}(\Lambda_1,xm)$, and $\ker\psi$ is cyclic of cardinality $N$ — the valuation subring of $e([x])$ is the preimage, under the inclusion of $\kappa(jq,jq_N)$ into the full modular function field of level $N$, of the valuation subring of the moduli place $\mathrm{moduliPlace}\,\kappa\,N\,W\,(\ker\psi)$ attached to the pair $(W,\ker\psi)$.
--
--   This is the level-$N$ form of the Deuring–Eichler dictionary at a supersingular vertex: classes in the class set of the Eichler order $R=\Lambda_1\cap m\widehat{\Lambda_1}m^{-1}$ of level $N$ correspond to supersingular points of the modular curve of level $N$ in characteristic $q'$, the correspondence being pinned down by the kernel-ideal description of any realisation $(W,\chi,d)$ of a class together with a cyclic $N$-isogeny $\psi$ and its dual. The dictionary clause is stated uniformly over all such realisations, so that it can be applied to realisations chosen elsewhere; it is used in the comparison of the degeneracy and Hecke structures on the two sides.
